      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ca74f3fb98a820b3ffec9cf|full_name}: This is partially not a bug. Earmuff mode was designed to target other player's avatars. If the audio source is attached to the exact center of your avatar then there's a good chance earmuff mode will read it as 0.0M away and not muffle it. If another player uses the same avatar and is outside of your range it will be correctly muffed. This is the case with the avatar linked in your comment.\nThe unmuffled avatar linked in your original post did indeed break Earmuffs though, so thank you for the report! It should be fixed in the next open beta.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
